      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A 12-pound cat eats two types of canned cat food: chicken flavored and duck-flavored. The\nrecommended amount of chicken-flavored food is 2.25 cans per 8 pounds of a cat’$s$ weight per\nday. The recommended amount of duck-flavored food is 1.75 cans per 9 pounds of a cat’$s$ weight\nper day. If $c$ is the number of chicken-flavored cans and $d$ is the number of duck flavored cans a\n12-pound cat eats in one day, which equation describes all the possible values of $c$ and $d$ for the\ncat to eat the recommended amount of food based on its weight?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-9ef2dff5413d4ce48eb510443ead13e6",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q7"
      },
      "options": [
        {
